     Under them the ACTION cells RRoott , MMiirr , NNaammee and DDuupp arm
     click-to-apply versions of the keys; IInn and OOuutt zoom (also +
     and - , and vv zooms to fit the whole drawing); FFrr and BBkk
     move the selection to the front or back of the stacking or-
     der; the LL_n cell cycles the ACTIVE layer new objects land
     on; and the < and > cells walk a numbered sheet set (the
     same actions as the < and > keys - see SHEET SETS).

     A SHAPE is placed by dragging its rectangle, then typing the
     label (drawn centred, clipped to the shape); shapes expose
     ATTACHMENT POINTS at their edge midpoints and corners.  A
     CONNECTOR is drawn with the wire gestures but snaps to at-
     tachment points and symbol pins, and STAYS ATTACHED: moving
     or resizing the target re-routes the connector.  The aarrrrooww
     and hhaarrrrooww styles carry an arrowhead at the far end.  The
     Arc cell draws a circular arc in two stages: drag from the
     centre to the start point, then click where the arc ends.
     The Net cell places a named net marker for the netlist ex-
     port.

     The DDiimm cell draws a DIMENSION point to point with the wire
     gestures; both ends snap to attachment points, so dimen-
     sioning a shape's edge is two clicks.  It lands on the an-
     notation layer, with extension ticks, arrowheads both ends
     and a centred label.  An EMPTY label is automatic: the
     measured distance times the sheet unit, integer formatted
     (``85 mm''); any text set through the style dialog overrides
     it, and emptying the text goes back to automatic.  The sheet
     unit (``one grid unit is 5 mm'') is set in Settings and
     saved in the drawing; coordinates stay grid units - only
     labels multiply.  A LEADER needs no tool of its own: an aarr-
     rrooww connector plus a text label already is one.

     The nn key (or the Name tool) edits a symbol's designator and
     value; on any other object it opens the STYLE dialog:
     solid/dashed/dotted line style, white/gray/black fill (fills
     stack in z-order), bold (width 2), HHaattcchh (a gray fill
     renders as 45-degree hatching - cross-section shading), the
     object's layer, its text and - for a text label - one of
     three sizes and VVeerrtt , which turns the label 90 degrees
     (axis labels, vertical dimensions).  A text label may hold
     several lines separated by `|'.  A polyline checked SSmmooootthh
     renders as a spline through its points, and -ppiicc exports it
     as one.

